Minutes: AKI after Cardiac Surgery and Protein Intake

Date: October 26, 2026 · Time: 4:30 pm · Location: Zoom Workplace
Present: Tom Baumann, Aymen Feki, Yassine Ben Ahmed, Ilyes Ihidheb, Jonas Ziegler, Johannes Piller, Prof. Dr. med. Wolfgang Hartl

Topics discussed

Introduction to acute kidney injury (AKI): symptoms, risk factors and prevention.
Effect of amino acid intake on kidney function.
Research question: Does the amount of amino acid intake after cardiac surgery have an impact on the development of AKI?
Statistical challenge: 10–15% of patients do not survive. For patients who die, the data cannot show whether protein intake would have affected kidney function (risk of selection bias).
Primary and secondary outcomes: new AKI diagnosed within the first 4 days after ICU admission vs. new AKI diagnosed on days 5–6 after ICU admission.
Patients with pre-existing AKI before surgery are excluded from the dataset.
Dataset: 350 patients, high data quality.
Randomized trials are strongly recommended as the gold standard for this type of question.

Decisions

Statistical questions: contact Johannes Piller.
Medical questions: contact Prof. Dr. Wolfgang Hartl.
Never push data to GitHub. Store it locally and exclude it from the repository via .gitignore.
Do not upload the data to any AI tools.
